From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 18 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tools/libbpf: const next_path in resolve_full_path (gcc 15)

The linux-headers postinst rebuilds tools/bpf/resolve_btfids in the target
rootfs. On resolute (gcc 15 / newer glibc) that build fails:

  tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c:11231: error: assignment discards 'const' qualifier
  from pointer target type [-Werror=discarded-qualifiers]
     next_path = strchr(s, ':');

's' is const char *, so strchr() yields const char *; assigning it to a plain
char * discards const. In the trixie build container (gcc <= 14) this is only
a warning, so the kernel artifact builds fine, but the postinst rebuild in the
resolute chroot is a hard error and the image build dies at
install_artifact_deb_chroot (linux-headers-current-phytium-embedded).

next_path is only read (pointer diff / NULL test), so make it const. Mainline
libbpf already carries this; the phytium-embedded 6.6 vendor kernel
(chainsx/phytium-linux-kernel, branch linux-6.6) still ships the pre-fix copy.
Scoped to that vendor kernel (phytiumpi).

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c b/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
+++ b/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
@@ -11223,7 +11223,7 @@ static int resolve_full_path(const char *file, char *result, size_t result_sz)
 		if (!search_paths[i])
 			continue;
 		for (s = search_paths[i]; s != NULL; s = strchr(s, ':')) {
-			char *next_path;
+			const char *next_path;
 			int seg_len;

 			if (s[0] == ':')
